module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.HomOutOfSupportedPushforward
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.RestrictComposite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedQCoh.SupportedDevissage
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedQCoh.SupportedPushforwardScheme
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.KoszulOrthogonality.AffineComparison
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.KoszulVanishing.OpenComplement

/-!
# Koszul detection across two opens: the hypotheses of the inductive step of Tag 09IS

Let `X` be a scheme covered by two opens `U` and `V`, with `V` affine — presented by an
isomorphism `e : V ≅ Spec A` — and let `f₁, …, f_r ∈ A` be equations cutting the closed set
`X ∖ U` out of `V`, that is with `e⁻¹(D(f₁) ∪ … ∪ D(f_r)) = U ∩ V`. Write `K` for the sheafified
Koszul complex of `f₁, …, f_r`, transported to `V`, and `Rj_{V*}K` for its derived pushforward to
`X`. This file proves the two geometric hypotheses the inductive step of [Stacks, Tag 09IS] and
[Stacks, Tag 0A9A] takes, namely those of
`Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_detection_of_prop`:

> `hKzero` : `(Rj_{V*}K)|_U = 0`, and
>
> `hdet` : an object `M` of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` with `M|_U = 0` which is right orthogonal to every
> shift of `Rj_{V*}K` is zero.

`hdet` is the statement [Stacks, Tag 09IR] supplies in the source's induction, read on `X` rather
than on the affine `V`. Its proof is the source's, in four steps.

* Right orthogonality to the shifts of `Rj_{V*}K` on `X` is right orthogonality to the shifts of
  `K` on `V`, by the Hom identification
  `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_derivedPushforward_iff`,
  whose support hypothesis is the second step below.
* `M|_V = 0`: this is [Stacks, Tag 09IR] on `Spec A`,
  `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero`, transported along `e`.
* `M|_U = 0` gives `(M|_V)|_{U ∩ V} = 0`, by
  `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isZero_derivedRestrict_of_range_le`.
* `M|_U = 0` and `M|_V = 0` give `M = 0`, by
  `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isZero_of_isZero_derivedRestrict_of_cover`.

`hKzero` is the support statement: `K` has cohomology supported on `V ∖ U`, which is the closed
set `X ∖ U`; derived pushforward along an open immersion preserves that support
([Stacks, Tag 08DF]), and a complex supported on `X ∖ U` restricts to zero on `U`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.koszulObjectOn` — the sheafified Koszul complex of `f₁, …, f_r`, read on
  `V` through the isomorphism `e : V ≅ Spec A`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.cohomologySupportedOn_koszulObjectOn` — its cohomology is supported on
  `X ∖ U`.
* `Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.isZero_derivedRestrict_derivedPushforward_koszulObjectOn` — **`hKzero`**:
  the derived pushforward of the Koszul object restricts to zero on `U`.
* `Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObjectOn_eq_zero` — [Stacks, Tag 09IR]
  transported from `Spec A` to `V`.
* `Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_derivedPushforward_koszulObjectOn` —
  **`hdet`**.

## Implementation notes

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. These are two of the inputs of [Stacks, Tag 09IS]; the tag
itself asserts that `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is generated by a single *perfect* object on a quasi-compact
quasi-separated scheme, and besides the inductive step needs the affine base case
(`Stacks.Duality.Affine.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_structureSheaf`), the extension of a perfect
object along [Stacks, Tag 09IQ], the induction principle [Stacks, Tag 08DR], and — to produce the
equations `f₁, …, f_r` this file takes as data — that a quasi-compact open of an affine scheme is
a finite union of principal opens.

**The model is the locally small one.** No `HasDerivedCategory` binder appears below, so instance
search supplies the global instances of
`StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/LocallySmall.lean`. This is forced, not chosen:
`Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero` passes through the affine
derived Spec–Γ equivalence of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0], which is available at that model and at no
other, and it is also the only model at which [Stacks, Tag 09IS] has content.

**Why the affine open is presented by an isomorphism rather than used directly.**
`Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero` is stated on
`Spec (CommRingCat.of A)` literally, while the Hom identification
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_derivedPushforward_iff` and
the two-open detection are stated for an open subscheme `V` of `X` and its inclusion `V.ι`.
Neither can be moved to the other's spelling, so the detection statement is carried across `e` by
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.derivedRestrictCompIsoId` and its two corollaries: restriction along
`e` reflects the zero object and, being faithful, reflects the vanishing of the morphisms out of
all shifts of an object.

**Three instance arguments are supplied as terms.** `Stacks.DerivedQCoh.cohomologySupportedOn_*`
are written with `ExtensionByZeroModules.jStar`, restriction of modules to an open *subspace*,
whose additivity and exactness are proved by exhibiting adjoints and are deliberately not
instances; and `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules X` and `SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf` are
definitionally but not reducibly equal, so synthesis does not cross between the spelling in which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor` is additive and the one those statements ask
about. The crossing between the two restriction functors on derived categories is
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.derivedJStarIsoRestrictFunctor`, and
`Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.jStar_eq_restrictFunctor` is the underlying equality of functors.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A9A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A9A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06Z0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06Z0)
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(R)` for sheaves of modules on a small site.
-- `D(𝒪_X)` for a scheme.
attribute [local instance] SheafOfModules.hasDerivedCategory
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty ExtensionByZeroModules
open Stacks.Cohomology
open Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel
open Stacks.Koszul.Truncation (koszulObject openComplement)

universe u

namespace Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (U V : X.Opens) {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
  (e : V.toScheme ≅ Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
  (hf : e.hom ⁻¹ᵁ openComplement f = V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U)

/-- **The Koszul object of `f₁, …, f_r` read on the affine open `V`.** It is the sheafified Koszul
complex `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.koszulObject` on `Spec A`, restricted along the isomorphism
`e : V ≅ Spec A`. -/
abbrev koszulObjectOn : DerivedCategory V.toScheme.Modules :=
  (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor e.hom).mapDerivedCategory.obj (koszulObject f)

/-- An object restricting to zero on `W` restricts to zero along `j` and then `g`, when the
composite `g ≫ j` of open immersions lands in `W`. -/
private theorem isZero_derivedRestrict_derivedRestrict_of_mem {Z Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Z ⟶ Y)
    (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsOpenImmersion g] [IsOpenImmersion j] (W : X.Opens)
    (hg : ∀ x : Z, (g ≫ j).base x ∈ W) {M : DerivedCategory X.Modules}
    (hM : IsZero ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor W.ι).mapDerivedCategory.obj M)) :
    IsZero ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor g).mapDerivedCategory.obj
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor j).mapDerivedCategory.obj M)) := by
  refine isZero_derivedRestrict_derivedRestrict_of_comp g j ?_
  refine isZero_derivedRestrict_of_range_le W _ ?_ hM
  rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
  exact hg x

include hf

/-- **The Koszul object on `V` restricts to zero on `U ∩ V`.** On `Spec A` the sheafified Koszul
complex restricts to zero on `D(f₁) ∪ … ∪ D(f_r)`, by
`Stacks.Koszul.OpenComplement.isZero_derivedRestrict_koszulObject`, and `e` carries `U ∩ V` into
that open by hypothesis. -/
theorem isZero_restrict_koszulObjectOn :
    IsZero ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι).mapDerivedCategory.obj
      (koszulObjectOn V e f)) := by
  refine isZero_derivedRestrict_derivedRestrict_of_mem (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι e.hom (openComplement f)
    (fun x => (SetLike.ext_iff.1 hf x.1).2 x.2)
    (Stacks.Koszul.OpenComplement.isZero_derivedRestrict_koszulObject f)

/-- **The cohomology of the Koszul object on `V` is supported on `X ∖ U`.** It restricts to zero
on `U ∩ V`, so its cohomology sheaves have vanishing stalks there, which is what support on the
complement of `U` says. -/
theorem cohomologySupportedOn_koszulObjectOn :
    PushforwardRestriction.CohomologySupportedOn V.toScheme.ringCatSheaf
      (Subtype.val ⁻¹' ((U : Set X)ᶜ)) (koszulObjectOn V e f) := by
  have hE : IsZero ((@Functor.mapDerivedCategory _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _
      (jStar (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U) V.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)
      (RingedSpace.restrictModules_additive V.toScheme.toRingedSpace (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U))
      (RingedSpace.restrictModules_preservesFiniteLimits V.toScheme.toRingedSpace (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U))
      (RingedSpace.restrictModules_preservesFiniteColimits V.toScheme.toRingedSpace
        (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U))).obj (koszulObjectOn V e f)) :=
    (isZero_restrict_koszulObjectOn U V e f hf).of_iso
      ((derivedJStarIsoRestrictFunctor V.toScheme (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U)).app (koszulObjectOn V e f))
  refine Stacks.DerivedQCoh.cohomologySupportedOn_mono _ ?_
    (@Stacks.DerivedQCoh.cohomologySupportedOn_compl_of_isZero_restrict _
      V.toScheme.ringCatSheaf (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U) (koszulObjectOn V e f)
      (RingedSpace.restrictModules_additive V.toScheme.toRingedSpace (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U))
      (RingedSpace.restrictModules_preservesFiniteLimits V.toScheme.toRingedSpace (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U))
      (RingedSpace.restrictModules_preservesFiniteColimits V.toScheme.toRingedSpace
        (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U)) hE)
  intro y hy
  exact hy

/-- **`hKzero`: the derived pushforward of the Koszul object restricts to zero on `U`.** The
cohomology of `K` is supported on the closed set `X ∖ U`, derived pushforward along the inclusion
of `V` preserves that support by [Stacks, Tag 08DF], and restriction to `U` pulls the supporting
set back to the empty set, where an object of the derived category vanishes.

This is the hypothesis `hKzero` of
`Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_detection_of_prop`. -/
theorem isZero_derivedRestrict_derivedPushforward_koszulObjectOn :
    IsZero ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor U.ι).mapDerivedCategory.obj
      ((Stacks.Duality.derivedPushforward V.ι).obj (koszulObjectOn V e f))) := by
  have hT : IsClosed ((U : Set X)ᶜ) := U.2.isClosed_compl
  have hsupp := Stacks.DerivedQCoh.cohomologySupportedOn_derivedPushforward_scheme X V
    ((U : Set X)ᶜ) hT (koszulObjectOn V e f) (cohomologySupportedOn_koszulObjectOn U V e f hf)
  have hL : PreservesFiniteLimits (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor U.ι) := inferInstance
  have hC : PreservesFiniteColimits (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor U.ι) := inferInstance
  have hpre := @Stacks.DerivedQCoh.cohomologySupportedOn_derivedRestriction _ X.ringCatSheaf U
    ((U : Set X)ᶜ) (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor U.ι)
    (Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.jStar_eq_restrictFunctor X U).symm
    (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor_additive U.ι) hL hC _ hsupp
  exact Stacks.DerivedQCoh.isZero_of_cohomologySupportedOn_empty _ _
    fun i y _ => hpre i y fun h => h y.2

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 09IR] on the affine open `V`.** An object `M` of `D(𝒪_V)` with quasi-coherent
cohomology sheaves which restricts to zero on `U ∩ V` and receives no nonzero morphism from a
shift of the Koszul object is zero.

This is `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero`, which is stated on
`Spec (CommRingCat.of A)` literally, carried across `e`. Restriction along `e.inv` sends `M` to an
object `N` of `D(𝒪_{Spec A})`; `N` has quasi-coherent cohomology because restriction along an open
immersion preserves quasi-coherence, it restricts to zero on `D(f₁) ∪ … ∪ D(f_r)` because `e`
carries that open into `U ∩ V`, and it receives no nonzero morphism from a shift of the Koszul
object because restriction along `e.hom` is faithful and commutes with the shift. So `N = 0`, and
restriction along `e.inv` reflects the zero object. -/
theorem isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObjectOn_eq_zero
    (M : DerivedCategory V.toScheme.Modules)
    (hM : DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := V.toScheme.Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent V.toScheme.ringCatSheaf) M)
    (hres : IsZero ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι).mapDerivedCategory.obj M))
    (h : ∀ (n : ℤ) (g : (koszulObjectOn V e f)⟦n⟧ ⟶ M), g = 0) :
    IsZero M := by
  have hmem : ∀ z : V.toScheme, e.hom.base z ∈ openComplement f → z ∈ V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U := by
    intro z hz
    rw [← hf]
    exact hz
  have hN : DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf)
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor e.inv).mapDerivedCategory.obj M) :=
    Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.derivedCategoryB_derivedRestrict e.inv M hM
  have hNres : IsZero ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor (openComplement f).ι).mapDerivedCategory.obj
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor e.inv).mapDerivedCategory.obj M)) := by
    refine isZero_derivedRestrict_derivedRestrict_of_mem (openComplement f).ι e.inv (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U)
      (fun x => hmem _ (by
        change e.hom.base (e.inv.base x.1) ∈ _
        simpa using x.2)) hres
  let := faithful_derivedRestrict_of_compEqId e.inv e.hom e.inv_hom_id
  have hNortho := forall_hom_shift_eq_zero_of_faithful
    (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor e.hom).mapDerivedCategory
    ((derivedRestrictCompIsoId e.hom e.inv e.hom_inv_id).app M) h
  exact isZero_of_isZero_derivedRestrict_of_compEqId e.hom e.inv e.hom_inv_id
    (Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero f _ hN hNres hNortho)

/-- **`hdet` for [Stacks, Tag 09IS].** Let `X` be covered by two opens `U` and `V`, with `V`
isomorphic to `Spec A` by `e`, and let `f₁, …, f_r ∈ A` cut `X ∖ U` out of `V`. An object `M` of
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` which restricts to zero on `U` and is right orthogonal to every shift of
`Rj_{V*}K`, for `K` the Koszul object of `f₁, …, f_r` on `V`, is zero.

This is the detection hypothesis of
`Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_detection_of_prop` at
`A = D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` and `K = Rj_{V*}K`, which is where [Stacks, Tag 09IR] is true: quantified over
all of `D(𝒪_X)` the hypothesis is false, and the quasi-coherence assumed here is exactly the
source's.

Orthogonality on `X` transfers to `M|_V` by
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_derivedPushforward_iff`, whose
support hypothesis is `Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.cohomologySupportedOn_koszulObjectOn`;
`M|_U = 0` gives `(M|_V)|_{U ∩ V} = 0`; so `M|_V = 0` by
`Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObjectOn_eq_zero`; and `M = 0` because `U` and
`V` cover `X`. -/
theorem isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_derivedPushforward_koszulObjectOn (hUV : U ⊔ V = ⊤)
    (M : DerivedCategory X.Modules)
    (hM : DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := X.Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent X.ringCatSheaf) M)
    (hMU : IsZero ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor U.ι).mapDerivedCategory.obj M))
    (hortho : ((singleton ((Stacks.Duality.derivedPushforward V.ι).obj
      (koszulObjectOn V e f))).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal M) :
    IsZero M := by
  have hcover : ∀ x : X, x ∈ U ∨ x ∈ V := by
    intro x
    have hx : x ∈ (⊤ : X.Opens) := trivial
    rw [← hUV] at hx
    exact hx
  have hT : IsClosed ((U : Set X)ᶜ) := U.2.isClosed_compl
  have hTV : ((U : Set X)ᶜ) ⊆ (V : Set X) := fun x hx => (hcover x).resolve_left hx
  have hMV := (rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_derivedPushforward_iff V
    ((U : Set X)ᶜ) hT hTV (koszulObjectOn V e f)
    (cohomologySupportedOn_koszulObjectOn U V e f hf) M).1 hortho
  have hMVres : IsZero ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι).mapDerivedCategory.obj
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor V.ι).mapDerivedCategory.obj M)) :=
    isZero_derivedRestrict_derivedRestrict_of_mem (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι V.ι U (fun x => x.2) hMU
  refine isZero_of_isZero_derivedRestrict_of_cover U V hcover hMU ?_
  exact isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObjectOn_eq_zero U V e f hf _
    (Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.derivedCategoryB_derivedRestrict V.ι M hM) hMVres
    ((rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_iff_forall_hom_eq_zero _ _).1 hMV)

end Stacks.Koszul.TwoOpens

end
